#
# Security region: build, hardened
#
# How the compiler builds the image's own programs (the shell, every tool,
# term, init). The kernel's regions harden the kernel; this one asks the same
# of the C that parses a peer's bytes, an archive and a terminal's input.
#
#   -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero   a local nobody wrote is zero, where it was
#                                  whatever the last call left on the stack:
#                                  the read of an uninitialised local stops
#                                  being an information leak and stops being
#                                  a value an attacker steered
#   -fstack-clash-protection       a frame or an alloca larger than a page is
#                                  probed a page at a time, so a request that
#                                  would step over the guard gap touches it
#   -fzero-call-used-regs=used-gpr every general register a function used is
#                                  cleared before it returns, so a gadget at
#                                  the return finds nothing it can use
#   -fstack-protector-strong       a function with an array or a local whose
#   -mstack-protector-guard=global address is taken puts a guard between them
#                                  and its return address and dies of SIGABRT
#                                  if the guard has changed when it returns;
#                                  lib.util.c sets the guard from getrandom at
#                                  the top of main and says so on stderr
#
# The cost, measured on a 9950X with the four flags against none on the shell
# (taskset to two cores, seven rounds of 1,500 starts, interleaved): a start of
# `sh -c :` is 37.0 us and becomes 39.1 (+5.7%); the three flags without the
# protector made it 37.5 (+1%). A loop of 20,000 shell arithmetic steps is
# inside the noise of the box it ran on (4.5 ms against 4.8 under a load of 10
# other jobs, the three-flag build faster than the plain one in the same run),
# and the program is 5.4% larger (4.35 MB to 4.59 MB before the packer). That
# is the reason these are a region and not the baseline. `MW_HARDEN=1 sh
# test/run LANE` builds a lane's programs with the same four flags.
#
# Not here, and why: -fcf-protection does nothing without a kernel that
# enforces user indirect branch tracking, and a program that is not position
# independent has no code to randomise (the Spark format has no relocations).
#
#> program_flags -ftrivial-auto-var-init=zero -fstack-clash-protection -fzero-call-used-regs=used-gpr -fstack-protector-strong -mstack-protector-guard=global
